course: dictionary
lesson: 4114
title: Gladly: willing and happy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When someone does something gladly, they do it willingly and with a happy heart. «I'll gladly help» means helping is a pleasure, not a chore. The words around it give the clue: "I'll" promises that help is coming, so gladly must show how the helper feels about it.
explain: Ask yourself: is this person happy to do it, or do they have to? Then test your meaning in the sentence. If «I'll gladly help» still makes sense with "happily" in place of gladly, you have found the meaning. Gladly is a polite way of saying yes.
explain: The vicar says, «a good secret ... will gladly be revealed». Here gladly shows that the good secret is willing to come out into the open, while a bad secret «fears the light» and hides. The word tells you how the secret feels about being shown.
fact: Gladly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Gladly» means willingly and happily, with pleasure.
fact: Useful phrases: «gladly help», «I would gladly», «gladly accept».
fact: In everyday talk, «I'll gladly help» is a polite way of agreeing.
fact: A good check is to swap in "willingly" or "happily" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «I'll gladly help you with your maths.» What does gladly mean here? | Quietly, in a whisper | Slowly and sadly | Angrily and loudly | *Willingly and happily
exercise: «I would gladly come with you to the park.» What does gladly show about the speaker? | *They want to go and are pleased to | They are lost and confused | They are too tired to move | They are unwilling to go
exercise: Tom says gladly means unwillingly. What is the right meaning? | *Willingly and with pleasure | Reluctantly, with a frown | Unwilling and cross | Sadly, without any choice
test: «The students gladly accept the new rules.» Which word is closest in meaning to gladly? | *Willingly | Angrily | Sleepily | Grudgingly
test: Which sentence uses gladly the right way? | The dog gladly hid under the bed. | *The volunteer gladly agreed to help clean the park. | The teacher gladly shouted at the class. | The boy gladly ate his cold, soggy peas.
exam: «She gladly accepted the invitation.» Which swap keeps the meaning the same? | Rudely | Sadly | *Happily | Reluctantly
